(a, e, i, o, u, y), but not if it is a diphthong or a double vowel or a vowel & r: *trapped, scrappy, uppish, popping, sleepy, carping, leaper.*
>>>

<<<
if their last syllable is accented (entrapped, but upheaped); they also double the p if, like handicap & kidnap, milksop & lollipop, they have a clear 4 or 6 as opposed to the obscure sound in jalap & gallop,
===
if their last syllable is accented (*entrapped*, but *upheaped*); they also double the *p* if, like *handicap* & *kidnap*, *milksop* & *lollipop*, they have a clear ă or ŏ as opposed to the obscure sound in *jalap* & *gallop*,
>>>

<<<
 or if, like horsewhip & sideslip, they are compounded with a monosyllable; but otherwise they do not double it except worship: chirruped, enveloping, galoping, galloper, gossipy, filliped, equipped,
===
 or if, like *horsewhip* & *sideslip*, they are compounded with a monosyllable; but otherwise they do not double it except *worship*: *chirruped, enveloping, galoping, galloper, gossipy, filliped, equipped,*
>>>

